{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/component/aspace_c55e62d8f5f99b198f04b32a823ee223","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"aspace_c55e62d8f5f99b198f04b32a823ee223","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Mabel Ludlum to and from various correspondents","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"abstract","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/abstract"}],"content":"Correspondence from Mabel Ludlum to various correspondents: 1. Letter to Mr. Macrae, Feb. 25, 1932, with six chapters of the manuscript by Amelia Martinez del Rio discussed in the letter. 2. Letter to Ethel Barr, Aug. 25, [1931], written on the back of a 1931 Essex County Garden Club flyer. 3. Letter to Ethel Barr, July 15, 1941. Correspondence from various correspondents to Mabel Ludlum: 1. Letter from Helen Chapman, Dec. 1929. 2. Letter from Margretta Stewart Dietrich, March 21, [no year, possibly 1933]. 3. Letter with an envelope, posted Jan. 7, 1937, from Theodora Goddard. The letter is dated Oct. 12, [1936, based on the postmark on the forwarding envelope.] 4. Letter from Anna Johnson, Aug. 8, 1937. 5. Postcard from \"Josephine\" [no last name and the postmark is illegible.] 6. Letter from Delia Stewart Lewis, undated.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":[],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":null,"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}